---
<Site title="Résumé — Aryaa Vijay"><div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><a class="back-link" href={path()}>← Back home</a><p class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE / EDUCATION / ENGINEERING</p><h1>Aryaa Vijay</h1><p class="lede">Aerospace engineering senior.<br/>GNC, CFD, and embedded systems.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={pdf} download>Download résumé ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href="mailto:avijay2024@my.fit.edu">Contact ↗</a></div><div class="resume-highlights"><span>GPA 3.8 / 4.0</span><span>Available May 2027</span><span>Florida Tech</span></div></header><div class="resume-grid"><section class="resume-summary"><p class="eyebrow">AT A GLANCE</p><h2>Education</h2><p><strong>Florida Institute of Technology</strong><br/>B.S. Aerospace Engineering · Expected May 2027<br/>GPA 3.8 / 4.0</p><h2>Availability</h2><p>Full-time roles or internships starting May 2027.</p><h2>Research experience</h2><p><strong>Undergraduate Research Assistant</strong><br/>Functional Biomaterials Lab, Florida Tech<br/>September 2025–April 2026</p><p>Precision sample preparation, 3D bioprinting equipment calibration and operation, and research documentation.</p><h2>Selected engineering work</h2><ul><li><a href={path('projects/pn-guidance/')}>3D PN / APN guidance simulation</a> — primary implementation and analysis; final 200-trial study</li><li><a href={path('projects/mach5-hypersonic-cfd/')}>Hypersonic aerodynamic analysis</a> — Mach 5, ANSYS Fluent</li><li><a href={path('projects/sard-drone/')}>S.A.R.D. drone</a> — independent hardware, vision, and sensor integration</li><li><a href={path('projects/flying-wing-glider/')}>Glider project</a> — project manager, team of four</li></ul><h2>Technical tools</h2><p>MATLAB · Python · ANSYS Fluent · NX Siemens · Onshape · KiCad · Git · LabVIEW · Raspberry Pi · Arduino</p><h2>Recognition</h2><p>Dean’s List: Fall 2024 and Fall 2025.</p></section><section class="resume-viewer" aria-label="Application résumé PDF"><ResumeViewer src={pdf} title="Aryaa Vijay résumé"/></section></div></div></Site>
